  "answer": "For irrigated wheat, urea timing depends on your agro-ecological zone [S2]. In lowland areas, apply urea in two equal splits: the first half after weeding when tillering starts, and the remaining half at the booting stage before flowering [S2]. In mid-altitude and highland areas, apply one-third of the urea at planting time [S2]. Apply the remaining two-thirds after weeding when tillering begins [S2].",
